  "cluster_id": 6,
  "patient": "Yeah, absolutely.",
  "therapist": "For this week, I want you to reflect on the reframe, kind of how the past is connected to what's going on now, but also how things would have turned out if you had just left that whole situation, how it might not be as positive for your siblings. So you contributed some good to a situation that was really miserable for you. And I also want you to try to, I've given you the thought record to work on for homework, I want you to try to capture that automatic thought when she yells at you. But think about how you can respond to the variety of automatic thoughts that you're having with adaptive responses, with the self-talk we talked about. There's still a real focus on the feelings, but in there is a thought. We believe that directly leads to them. So what I want to work on with you is interrupting that process and let's see what's actually happening at the cognition level before just to the feeling, and see if we can get some self-talk in there. If you can complete one to three thought records on that. Remember to ask yourself that question, 'What's going through my mind right now?' so when that yelling starts, try to maintain focus and say 'What's going through my mind right now?' Think about that thought that's automatically coming into your mind, and then we can build some adaptive responses, some self-talk.",
